cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it as below. The source texts it holds
  are not the project's own: cite each from its record, as DATA_RIGHTS.md
  explains.
title: "Mundus Ulterior"
abstract: >-
  A research portal on ancient Rome seen from beyond its frontiers, 27 BC to
  1204 AD. It holds 54 source records from seven regions, in their original
  languages beside published translations, and prepared questions whose
  archived answers quote those sources and are re-checked against them. It
  adds a map of the places the sources name, and a full account of the
  method and of what did not work.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Padilla
    given-names: Rob
repository-code: "https://github.com/productofrob/mundus-ulterior"
url: "https://mundus-ulterior.pages.dev/"
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - ancient history
  - Roman Empire
  - cross-lingual retrieval
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - citation
  - provenance
